1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:01,740
Why is the sky blue?

2
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:03,740
The answer is hiding inside

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:06,000
sunlight.

4
00:00:06,290 --> 00:00:08,730
Sunlight looks white, but it is really

5
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:10,720
every color of the rainbow traveling

6
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:12,000
together.

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,740
Each color is a wave.

8
00:00:14,290 --> 00:00:16,970
Red waves are long and lazy.

9
00:00:16,970 --> 00:00:19,970
Blue waves are short and choppy.

10
00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:22,970
When sunlight hits the air, tiny molecules

11
00:00:23,010 --> 00:00:25,000
bounce the short waves in every direction,

12
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,030
while long waves mostly pass straight

13
00:00:28,030 --> 00:00:29,000
through.

14
00:00:29,290 --> 00:00:32,260
Blue light scatters about six times more

15
00:00:32,290 --> 00:00:33,000
than red.

16
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,970
So blue reaches your eyes from every part

17
00:00:36,010 --> 00:00:37,000
of the sky.

18
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,890
Red light has a wavelength near 700

19
00:00:39,890 --> 00:00:41,000
nanometers.

20
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Blue is around 450.

21
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,720
Shorter wave, stronger

22
00:00:46,690 --> 00:00:46,970
scattering.

23
00:00:46,970 --> 00:00:49,760
Violet scatters even more, so why isn't

24
00:00:49,810 --> 00:00:51,000
the sky violet?

25
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,700
The sun sends out less of it, the upper

26
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:56,260
atmosphere absorbs some, and our eyes are

27
00:00:56,260 --> 00:00:57,970
less sensitive to it.

28
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,970
At sunset, light crosses far more air.

29
00:01:01,970 --> 00:01:04,860
The blue gets scattered away, and red is

30
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:06,000
what is left.

31
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Now you know.

32
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:09,730
Follow for more.
